<code>assert (e == null) => (this.getLast() == null); assert (e != null) => (this.getLast().equals(e));</code>

However, since we need to combine these conditions into a single assert statement, we can use the conditional operator:

<code>assert (e == null) == (this.getLast() == null);</code>

This single assert statement captures both conditions: if `e` is null, then the last element of the list should be null, and if `e` is not null, then the last element of the list should be equal to `e`.
